{
  "_readme": [
    "Scenario configurations for the MBO monetary policy model.",
    "",
    "EVERY NUMBER IN THIS FILE IS ILLUSTRATIVE AND NON-NORMATIVE. None of it is",
    "a policy proposal, a recommendation, or a protocol parameter.",
    "",
    "CURRENT SCOPE - READ THIS BEFORE DRAWING ANY CONCLUSION.",
    "",
    "Every scenario below shares the same primary issuance schedule:",
    "initial_annual_issuance 3153600, step_years 5, step_factor 0.5.",
    "Those three values are taken from the emission schedule documented in",
    "docs/supply_schedule.md (0.1 MBO per block, halving every five years).",
    "",
    "Consequently this scenario set does NOT explore the primary-issuance",
    "design space. It holds the documented schedule constant and compares only",
    "what happens AFTER it: hard-cap termination, fixed tail, percentage tail,",
    "an experimental adaptive tail, and adoption/stress assumptions.",
    "",
    "In particular, base is NOT a neutral monetary baseline. It is an",
    "illustrative benchmark anchored on the documented historical schedule.",
    "",
    "historical_documented_partial is a PARTIAL reconstruction; see the",
    "fidelity notes attached to that scenario."
  ],

  "scenarios": {
    "historical_documented_partial": {
      "description": "PARTIAL reconstruction of the emission schedule documented in docs/supply_schedule.md. Documented, NOT implemented, and NOT a faithful reconstruction of the documented fee system.",
      "normative": false,
      "provenance": "docs/supply_schedule.md, docs/monetary_policy.md, docs/token_distribution.md",
      "fidelity": [
        "FAITHFUL: primary issuance schedule (0.1 MBO per block, 3153600 per year,",
        "halving every 5 years) and the 31536000 cumulative issuance cap.",
        "",
        "NOT FAITHFUL: the fee system. docs/economic_summary.md describes two fee",
        "channels - base fee burned, priority fee routed to validators and compute",
        "providers - and does not state the ratio between them. This simulator has a",
        "single aggregate fee pool and cannot represent two channels.",
        "",
        "burn_share 1.0 therefore models the documented base-fee burn channel only.",
        "The priority-fee channel is absent, so validator_fee_revenue is 0 here by",
        "construction. Validator fee revenue and the security budget in this",
        "scenario MUST NOT be read as a faithful reconstruction of the documented",
        "historical security budget: they understate it by the whole priority-fee",
        "channel. No base/priority ratio has been invented to fill the gap."
      ],
      "monetary": {
        "family": "hard_cap",
        "initial_supply": 0,
        "cap": 31536000,
        "primary_emission": {
          "initial_annual_issuance": 3153600,
          "step_years": 5,
          "step_factor": 0.5,
          "phase_end_year": null
        }
      },
      "supply_distribution": { "circulating_fraction": 0.85, "staking_ratio": 0.45 },
